    text: "---"
  - line: 18
    type: narration
    text: "scene 015.5 — departure and legacy"
  - line: 20
    type: narration
    text: "scene meta:"
  - line: 21
    type: narration
    text: "location: Orbital Observation Aperture (Crimson Citadel)"
  - line: 22
    type: narration
    text: "time: year 10,550, month 6, day 21"
  - line: 23
    type: narration
    text: "participants: Queen Eduhauana"
  - line: 24
    type: narration
    text: "focus: Queen Eduhauana conducts a final tactical assessment of the Second Coming, notes the elimination of entry-level biological assets, confirms Ash Giant collaboration, outlines long-term projections for the Third, Fourth, and Fifth Comings, and authorizes orbital departure."
  - line: 25
    type: narration
    text: "continuity: 4 months, 7 days after the discovery of betrayal in scene 015.4"
  - line: 26
    type: narration
    text: "presentation: cutscene"
  - line: 27
    type: narration
    text: "cutscene purpose: Queen Eduhauana's orbital assessment of the Second Coming and the departure of the Crimson Citadel."
  - line: 29
    type: narration
    text: "Queen Eduhauana stood before the observation aperture one final time, reviewing the Second Coming's outcomes with satisfaction that three thousand years of patience had earned."
  - line: 31
    type: narration
    text: "The Nephilim manifestation had been unexpected—evidence that the Aeon Keepers maintained more influence than her initial assessments suggested."
  - line: 32
    type: narration
    text: "But the convergence itself had served her purposes perfectly."
  - line: 33
    type: narration
    text: "The ritual's success had fractured Giant unity more completely than military conquest ever could."
  - line: 35
    type: narration
    text: "Tactical assessment:"
  - line: 36
    type: narration
    text: "- Gruulith, Dregan forces: eliminated by Nephilim countermeasures."
  - line: 37
    type: narration
    text: "Acceptable losses—they were entry-level assets designed for pressure application, not sustained occupation."
  - line: 38
    type: narration
    text: "- Brajor: eliminated despite defection attempt."
  - line: 39
    type: narration
    text: "Demonstrates consequences of choosing resistance over cooperation."
  - line: 40
    type: narration
    text: "Perfect object lesson for future deployments."
  - line: 41
    type: narration
    text: "- Ash Giant collaboration secured: 23% of mountain territories now under cooperative administration."
  - line: 42
    type: narration
    text: "Intelligence gathering operational."
  - line: 43
    type: narration
    text: "- Remaining tribes: fragmented, isolated, mutual trust degraded beyond near-term recovery."
  - line: 44
    type: narration
    text: "Unity impossible without generational healing that occupation will prevent."
  - line: 46
    type: narration
    text: "Long-term projections:"
  - line: 47
    type: narration
    text: "- Third Coming (in 3,500 cycles): Deploy ice-age protocols, test whether environmental catastrophe prompts cooperation or accelerates fragmentation."
  - line: 48
    type: narration
    text: "Probability matrices suggest fragmentation."
  - line: 49
    type: narration
    text: "- Fourth Coming (7,000 cycles hence): Introduce human populations as intermediate management layer."
  - line: 50
    type: narration
    text: "Giants' pride will prevent cooperation with \"lesser\" species, ensuring continued isolation."
  - line: 51
    type: narration
    text: "- Fifth Coming (10,500 cycles total): Complete network activation."
  - line: 52
    type: narration
    text: "Harvest fully matured bloodline assets (if Tran/Viên genetic lines develop as projected)."
  - line: 53
    type: narration
    text: "Indigenous resistance capability: minimal, due to self-imposed fragmentation sustained across four occupation cycles."
  - line: 55
    type: dialogue
    speaker: Eduhauana
    text: "\"Departure authorization,\""
  - line: 57
    type: narration
    text: "The Crimson Citadel began its slow ascent toward departure trajectory."
  - line: 58
    type: narration
    text: "Behind them, the planet turned—blue and green and beautiful, its indigenous populations now divided beyond any hope of unity, their resistance broken not through military defeat but through patient exploitation of their own capacity for mistrust."
  - line: 60
    type: narration
    text: "The Second Coming was complete."
  - line: 62
    type: narration
    text: "The Sundering was permanent."
  - line: 64
    type: narration
    text: "And in the cold mathematics of cosmic conquest, this victory was more absolute than any battlefield triumph could achieve."
  - line: 66
    type: scene_header
    text: "---"
  - line: 68
    type: narration
    text: "Year 10,550, Month 7, Day 1"

